TITLE:: PV_PolyFreqWarp
summary:: Polynomial frequency warping of spectral data
categories:: UGens>FFT

DESCRIPTION::
PV_PolyFreqWarp applies polynomial frequency warping to an incoming FFT spectrum. Spectral peaks are detected and tracked across frames to maintain phase coherence during transformation.


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Apply polynomial frequency warping to an FFT buffer.

ARGUMENT:: buffer
The input FFT buffer (e.g., produced by link::Classes/FFT::).

ARGUMENT:: curve0
Polynomial coefficient for 5th order warping term.

ARGUMENT:: curve1
Polynomial coefficient for 4th order warping term.

ARGUMENT:: curve2
Polynomial coefficient for 3rd order warping term.

ARGUMENT:: curve3
Polynomial coefficient for 2nd order warping term.

ARGUMENT:: scale
Linear frequency scaling factor (default 1.0). Scaling by a factor equates to pitch transposition (e.g. 2.0 transposes up one octave, 0.5 transposes down one octave, and 1.0 preserves original pitch).

ARGUMENT:: shift
Global frequency shift in normalized frequency units (where 1.0 corresponds to shifting across the entire spectrum up to the Nyquist frequency, and -1.0 shifts down by Nyquist; default is 0.0).

ARGUMENT:: reflect
Whether to reflect spectral components at DC and Nyquist (1 = reflect with phase conjugation, 0 = clip). Default is 1.

ARGUMENT:: detector
Optional FFT buffer used for peak and magnitude detection instead of code::buffer::. Pass code::nil:: (or omit) to use code::buffer:: itself. When processing multichannel signals (e.g. stereo), a shared detector chain (such as the FFT of a summed or linked mix) can be passed to all channel instances. This ensures identical peak detection and spectral region boundaries across channels, maintaining inter-channel phase coherence and stereo imaging.

ARGUMENT:: overlap
FFT overlap factor (e.g., 4 for hop ratio 0.25). Default is 4. Below 4 is liable to have significant amplitude modulation.

returns:: The processed FFT chain.


EXAMPLES::

code::
(
s.waitForBoot {
    b = Buffer.read(s, Platform.resourceDir +/+ "sounds/a11wlk01.wav");
    s.sync;

    x = {
        var in, chain, sig;
        in = PlayBuf.ar(1, b, BufRateScale.kr(b), loop: 1);
        chain = FFT(LocalBuf(4096), in);
        chain = PV_PolyFreqWarp(
            buffer: chain,
            scale: MouseX.kr(0.5, 2.0, \exponential),
            shift: MouseY.kr(-0.5, 0.5)
        );
        sig = IFFT(chain);
        sig ! 2 * 0.2;
    }.play;
};
)

x.free;
b.free;
::
